# What must never enter the build context.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything left out of this file is copied
# into the build stage — and `vite build` *inlines* every VITE_* variable it can
# see into the JavaScript nginx then serves. Without this file a developer's
# `.env.local` was baked into the image: the real Supabase project, and a real
# PostHog key on a container answering at http://localhost:3000. That is where
# 16 of the 19 phantom PostHog people came from. Configuration for a container
# build is passed explicitly with --build-arg instead; see the Dockerfile.

# Secrets and machine-local configuration. `.env.example` holds names, not
# values, and is the one that documents what a build needs.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Rebuilt inside the image, or irrelevant to it.
node_modules
dist
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
e2e
.git
.gitignore
.github
.worktrees

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
